WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.890
- The fans want more,

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:03.880
so we're going to do something
we call "Audience Ask".

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.109
- Oh Lordy.
- Are you ready?

00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:05.942
- Mhm.

00:00:05.942 --> 00:00:06.775
(plucking string instrument)
- [Kelly] There ya go.

00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:09.210
So where is Latisha?

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.117
Oh hi, Latisha.

00:00:10.117 --> 00:00:12.318
(applause)
I heard you singin'.

00:00:12.318 --> 00:00:13.151
- Oh, thank you!

00:00:13.151 --> 00:00:15.390
- I know, Latisha can sing, I
heard her on commercial break.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.223
- Oh, you can sin--

00:00:16.223 --> 00:00:17.340
- So what do you wanna ask Lisa?

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.340
- So uh, Kelly, so nice to meet you.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.173
Lisa nice to meet you.

00:00:20.173 --> 00:00:21.995
Andy and Buffy, what's good?

00:00:21.995 --> 00:00:23.110
(laughter)

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:25.530
So the question I had for you is;

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:26.770
If you had to be locked in a room

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:28.270
with any of the Real House Wives,

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.320
who would it be and what
would you talk about

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:31.420
to make the time pass?

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.960
- Wow!
- Oh my goodness!

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.900
That's not fair since I just left.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.500
Oh, it could be from
any of the franchises.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.660
- It could be from any of the franchises.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.580
- Um, I think probably Bethany,

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.570
but I probably wouldn't have
to discuss anything with her

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:42.920
'cause I wouldn't get a word in edgewise.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.653
Because--
(laughter)

00:00:45.653 --> 00:00:46.486
uh, yeah.
- [Kelly] You're so mean.

00:00:46.486 --> 00:00:48.260
- Yeah, so, probably Bethany.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.973
- That's awesome, well thank
you Latisha (applause).

00:00:49.973 --> 00:00:50.806
- Thank you.
- [Kelly] Thank you

00:00:50.806 --> 00:00:51.639
for warmin' it up.

00:00:51.639 --> 00:00:53.540
- We have another question.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:54.746
Here we go.

00:00:54.746 --> 00:00:55.579
(plucking string instrument)

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:57.250
- Where is Brenna?

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.083
Brenna.

00:00:58.083 --> 00:00:58.950
Hi Brenna.
(applause)

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.427
- Thank you.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.130
So, I actually have two questions.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.681
- Okay-- greedy, but okay.

00:01:03.681 --> 00:01:05.170
(chuckles)

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.500
the first one is;

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.460
do you think that Stassi and Kristen

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.870
are gonna be able to mend things?

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.550
- Well, I think, fundamentally,

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.370
there's been a difference between them.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:17.430
I mean, I try not to weigh in
on this too much, personally,

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.320
because I've always found
Kristen a little difficult

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.040
to get on with, myself.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.300
But I think this year Stass has grown up--

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.900
They both have grown up, I have to say.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.730
She's got a book deal now, Kristen.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.500
And Stassi's, you know, getting married

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.520
and should be on the
best sellers list, so,

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.353
they're both growing up,

00:01:33.353 --> 00:01:35.640
but I think the divide
just got wider and wider

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.520
and I don't know, but
there's years of history,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.480
so I'm hopeful.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.010
Because it's a shame to break
up such a long friendship.

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:45.840
But, I don't know, this
season it was very bumpy,

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:46.880
very bumpy.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:47.770
- [Lisa] Fingers crossed.
- [Kelly] Drama!

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:48.603
- Thank you
- [Lisa] Yeah.

00:01:48.603 --> 00:01:49.436
- [Kelly] All right.

00:01:49.436 --> 00:01:50.370
What's the second question, greedy?

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.530
- And what do you think the deal is

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.680
with Jax unfollowing everybody?

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:56.513
Is he trying to stir the pot, or?

00:01:56.513 --> 00:01:57.770
- Oh, I cannot spill that one,

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:01.350
because that kinda comes
at the end of the season.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.480
- Oh, she's trying to get you to--

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:03.550
- Yeah, you are!

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:06.570
Like, who's she working for, exactly!

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.010
I can't give that away
otherwise I would be in--

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:12.130
but you know, Jax he's very complicated,

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:13.451
complicated character.

00:02:13.451 --> 00:02:15.240
(clicks tongue)
- He sounds fun.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.430
- He's a-- that is bad!

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.263
(laughter)

